solutions.latex:
\exfigure{1342_q29_s1}

The curves intersect where $e^x=6-8e^{-x}$, so $e^x=6-\dfrac{8}{e^x}$, $e^{2x}=6e^x-8$, hence $e^{2x}-6e^x+8=0$.

$(e^x-2)(e^x-4)=0$, so $e^x=2$ or $e^x=4$, giving $x_1=\ln2,\ x_2=\ln4$.
